# Android / Gradle build output.
#
# Worth being explicit about the scale: across the four projects, 1,240 of
# 1,414 files are build artifacts -- 65.5 MB of 66.0 MB. The actual source is
# about 0.1 MB per project. Committing the build directory would make every
# repo 300x larger than it needs to be, and every rebuild would show as a
# diff of hundreds of regenerated binaries.
build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class

# Android Studio / IntelliJ. The IDE rewrites most of these on every open,
# so they are pure churn -- except the two below, which are kept on purpose
# because they define the project for anyone else who opens it.
.idea/
!.idea/codeStyles/
!.idea/inspectionProfiles/
*.iml
.navigation/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/

# local.properties holds the absolute path to THIS machine's Android SDK.
# It is regenerated on first open and is wrong for every other machine.
local.properties

# Signing material. Never commit these -- a keystore plus its password is
# the ability to publish an update that Android will accept as genuinely
# yours.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
